groupbar: draw the gradients from textures one pixel wide

renderGradient() draws each of the four group bar gradients (active,
inactive, locked active, locked inactive) into a texture the size of the
focused monitor. The gradient is vertical, from (0, 0) to (0, height), and
the same in every column, and the whole texture is stretched over each
tab's box: one column of the same height draws the same pixels.

A monitor-sized RGBA texture is 35 MiB at 3840x2400 (40 MiB as Mesa's iris
rounds it up), so the four held 160 MiB, made at every config load with
group:groupbar:gradients on, whether or not a group is open; each reload
freed and made them again. One column of 2400 is 9.4 KiB.

In a nested Hyprland at 3840x2400, with gradients on and no window, the
render node's DRM fdinfo said 607.6 to 609.6 MiB before and 375.1 to 375.2
after (three runs each); with two windows in a group, 850.0 and 697.8. A
picture of the grouped windows is the same before and after, pixel for
pixel.

--- a/src/render/decorations/CHyprGroupBarDecoration.cpp
+++ b/src/render/decorations/CHyprGroupBarDecoration.cpp
@@ -324,7 +324,11 @@
     if (!Desktop::focusState()->monitor())
         return nullptr;
 
-    const Vector2D& bufferSize = Desktop::focusState()->monitor()->m_transformedSize;
+    // The gradient runs from the top down and is the same all across, and the
+    // texture is stretched over each tab: one column of the monitor's height
+    // draws the same tabs. A texture the monitor's size took 35 MiB a color at
+    // 3840x2400, four of them whether or not any group is open.
+    const Vector2D  bufferSize = {1.0, Desktop::focusState()->monitor()->m_transformedSize.y};
 
     const auto      CAIROSURFACE = cairo_image_surface_create(CAIRO_FORMAT_ARGB32, bufferSize.x, bufferSize.y);
     const auto      CAIRO        = cairo_create(CAIROSURFACE);
